From: Surface RT bring-up
Subject: [PATCH 19] grate: keep final varying values in pixel rows and stream direct products

Nonconstant varying values held in the global register bank can become
block-constant during recirculation. The original perspective MUL test
fails 821/1024 pixels despite passing on llvmpipe.

Allow a final single-input fetch to use the now-consumed pixel row.
Pack a canonical RGBA row in B,A,R,G order to avoid overwriting an unread
FP20 value while producing packed BGRA in R2/R3.

For direct two-varying products, link each selected source component into
separate TRAM slots. Fetch the two scalar operands together into R0/R1,
accumulate packed output in R2/R3 and store only after the last component.
This avoids a persistent global-register scratch without changing pixel
row capacity or PSEQ flow control. Preserve swizzles and input modifiers.
General multi-input temporary allocation remains incomplete.

Applies after 0018. The original perspective test and four additional
nonconstant varying cases pass on Tegra with the existing pixel tolerance.

